I agree that the enforcement can go to ridiculous lengths, but I can
also understand the desire of news sites to eliminate the *obvious*
violations of the law.  It's one thing if a single posting in some
unrelated newsgroup touches on taboo subjects; it's quite another to
carry a newsgroup dedicated to that purpose.  

You're right -- the law doesn't make much sense -- but I can sympathize
with folks who are not in a position to test the waters for change.  In 
this case, that battle is one *much* better fought by the traditional media.
What have the traditional media been doing about this law in recent years?

Electronic media, still in its infancy, is not the place to force change
in laws written for traditional print media.

