>
>     Group               Length         Diameter
>
>     Orientals           4 - 5.5"       1.25"
>     Caucasians          5.5 - 6"       1.3 - 1.6"
>     Blacks              6.25 - 8"      2"
>
>Clitoral lengths:
>     Europeans 1.2"
>     Africans 2".


(I address this to the FAQ author but post it out of general interest)

You might want to reconsider using these figures or at least put a
caveat with them.  Professor Rushton is, to say the least, highly
controversial and many think he's just nuts and his work is worthless.

There was a major stink-up in Canada a few years back when it was reported
that Rushton had published work suggesting that there was statisticly
proven differences among major race groups in average I.Q. and other 
characteristics, such as male penis lengths.  In particular, he found
that Orientals tended to score higher than Caucasians who scored higher
on average than Blacks.

Not surprisingly, he was widely denounced as a racist and there were
called for him to be turfed out of his chair at Western.  Students
boycotted his classes.  He protested that he was not trying to be
racist, but merely reporting scientifically the results of his research.
I think many (myself included) felt that even if you partly accepted 
that his work might have some scientific validity, that it had a
certain "odour".   He seemed in his methods - correlating racial I.Q. 
with penis size, etc. - to be deliberately trying to prove many racist 
stereotypes.

Of particular relevance to the Alt.Sex FAQ and the figures quoted above,
many other researchers criticised his methods and complained that his
figures were simply wrong and his results scientifically worthless.  In
one famous episode he was challenged to a public debate by Dr. David
Suzuki, Canada's best known "media-scientist" and a respected geneticist.
Rushton accepted and from what I heard, Suzuki thoroughly trashed
Rushton and the attack was based mainly on the mistakes in Rushton's
research methods.

This affair was an early example of something that's been happening
more frequently in Canada of late: University professors coming out
with politically unacceptable views and being criticised by the
more politically correct who call for his or her dismissal.  This
has sparked a National debate on academic freedom and freedom of
expression in general.

As far as I know, Rushton's still at Western...I've no idea what he's
been up to and if he's keeping a "lower profile" these days!  Perhaps
others can correct any mistakes I've made above (I wasn't there and I'm
going from memory) and fill us in on any subsequent developments.


Let me stress that I'm not saying that Rushton's figures should not
appear in the Alt.Sex FAQ because they are not politically correct
or because they are the work of an alleged racist but rather because
they may be quite bogus and the result of flawed research.  At least
there should be a footnote saying that the figures are disputed.


Thank you for you time.  Note that I have cross-posted this so if
you follow up, please consider editing the Followup-To: line.

